    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not an optimal schedule. It always produces a valid output, but I have not compiled or run it against the real data sets.\n\n**Approach:**\n1. **Assign each order's items to warehouses.** For each order and product type, the items are taken from the nearest warehouse that still has stock. The stock is reserved immediately, so no warehouse is over-committed. The result is a set of groups `(warehouse, product, order, count)`.\n2. **Schedule trips.** The drone with the earliest free time picks the group with the lowest time per delivered item. A trip is a Load at the warehouse followed by a Deliver to the order, carrying as many items as the payload allows. A trip is only added if it finishes by the deadline `T`. A drone with no feasible group is retired.\n\nThe output is built per drone, so each drone's commands are in chronological order.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Group { int w, p, o, cnt; };\n\nstatic long long ceilDist(long long r1, long long c1, long long r2, long long c2) {\n    long long dr = r1 - r2, dc = c1 - c2;\n    long long d2 = dr * dr + dc * dc;\n    if (d2 == 0) return 0;\n    long long n = (long long)sqrtl((long double)d2);\n    while (n * n < d2) n++;\n    while (n > 0 && (n - 1) * (n - 1) >= d2) n--;\n    return n;\n}\n\nstatic int readInt() {\n    int c = getchar();\n    while (c != '-' && (c < '0' || c > '9')) c = getchar();\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar(); }\n    int x = 0;\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') { x = x * 10 + (c - '0'); c = getchar(); }\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int R = readInt(), Cc = readInt(), D = readInt(), T = readInt(), maxL = readInt();\n    int P = readInt();\n    vector<int> wt(P);\n    for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) wt[i] = readInt();\n\n    int W = readInt();\n    vector<int> wr(W), wc(W);\n    vector<vector<uint16_t>> stock(W, vector<uint16_t>(P));\n    for (int w = 0; w < W; w++) {\n        wr[w] = readInt();\n        wc[w] = readInt();\n        for (int p = 0; p < P; p++) stock[w][p] = (uint16_t)readInt();\n    }\n    // warehouses with stock per product\n    vector<vector<int>> prodWh(P);\n    for (int p = 0; p < P; p++)\n        for (int w = 0; w < W; w++)\n            if (stock[w][p] > 0) prodWh[p].push_back(w);\n\n    int C = readInt();\n    vector<int> orr(C), occ(C);\n    vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> orderNeeds(C); // (product, count)\n    for (int o = 0; o < C; o++) {\n        orr[o] = readInt();\n        occ[o] = readInt();\n        int L = readInt();\n        vector<int> items(L);\n        for (int i = 0; i < L; i++) items[i] = readInt();\n        sort(items.begin(), items.end());\n        for (int i = 0; i < L;) {\n            int j = i;\n            while (j < L && items[j] == items[i]) j++;\n            orderNeeds[o].push_back({items[i], j - i});\n            i = j;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Step 1: assign items to nearest warehouses with stock\n    vector<Group> groups;\n    for (int o = 0; o < C; o++) {\n        for (auto [p, n0] : orderNeeds[o]) {\n            int n = n0;\n            auto &lst = prodWh[p];\n            while (n > 0) {\n                // remove exhausted warehouses\n                for (size_t i = 0; i < lst.size();) {\n                    if (stock[lst[i]][p] == 0) {\n                        lst[i] = lst.back();\n                        lst.pop_back();\n                    } else i++;\n                }\n                if (lst.empty()) break; // should not happen by guarantee\n                int best = -1; long long bd = LLONG_MAX;\n                for (int w : lst) {\n                    long long d = ceilDist(orr[o], occ[o], wr[w], wc[w]);\n                    if (d < bd || (d == bd && w < best)) { bd = d; best = w; }\n                }\n                int a = min<int>(n, stock[best][p]);\n                stock[best][p] -= a;\n                n -= a;\n                groups.push_back({best, p, o, a});\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Step 2: schedule drones\n    vector<long long> dt(D, 0);\n    vector<int> dr(D, wr.empty() ? 0 : wr[0]), dc(D, wc.empty() ? 0 : wc[0]);\n    vector<bool> active(D, true);\n    vector<vector<string>> cmds(D);\n\n    while (true) {\n        int d = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < D; i++)\n            if (active[i] && (d == -1 || dt[i] < dt[d])) d = i;\n        if (d == -1 || groups.empty()) break;\n\n        int bestI = -1;\n        double bestVal = 1e18;\n        long long bestTotal = 0;\n        int bestK = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < (int)groups.size(); i++) {\n            const Group &g = groups[i];\n            int cap = maxL / wt[g.p];\n            int k = min(cap, g.cnt);\n            if (k <= 0) continue;\n            long long d1 = ceilDist(dr[d], dc[d], wr[g.w], wc[g.w]);\n            long long d2 = ceilDist(wr[g.w], wc[g.w], orr[g.o], occ[g.o]);\n            long long total = dt[d] + d1 + 1 + d2 + 1;\n            if (total > T) continue;\n            double val = (double)(d1 + d2 + 2) / k;\n            if (val < bestVal) {\n                bestVal = val;\n                bestI = i;\n                bestTotal = total;\n                bestK = k;\n            }\n        }\n        if (bestI == -1) {\n            active[d] = false;\n            continue;\n        }\n        Group g = groups[bestI];\n        cmds[d].push_back(to_string(d) + \" L \" + to_string(g.w) + \" \" + to_string(g.p) + \" \" + to_string(bestK));\n        cmds[d].push_back(to_string(d) + \" D \" + to_string(g.o) + \" \" + to_string(g.p) + \" \" + to_string(bestK));\n        dt[d] = bestTotal;\n        dr[d] = orr[g.o];\n        dc[d] = occ[g.o];\n        groups[bestI].cnt -= bestK;\n        if (groups[bestI].cnt == 0) {\n            groups[bestI] = groups.back();\n            groups.pop_back();\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long Q = 0;\n    for (int d = 0; d < D; d++) Q += cmds[d].size();\n    string out;\n    out += to_string(Q) + \"\\n\";\n    for (int d = 0; d < D; d++)\n        for (auto &s : cmds[d]) { out += s; out += '\\n'; }\n    fputs(out.c_str(), stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
